---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice | Hyperboards"
  description="A pre-launch overview of the information Hyperboards expects to collect through this website and how it is intended to be handled."
  noindex={true}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="A careful approach to the information you share."
    intro="This page describes the intended handling of website inquiries while the final legal entity, privacy contact and jurisdiction-specific terms are being confirmed."
    marker="P"
  />

  <section class="section legal-page">
    <div class="container">
      <aside class="legal-status" role="note" aria-labelledby="privacy-status-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Pre-launch status</p>
        <h2 id="privacy-status-title">This is a general interim notice, not a final privacy policy.</h2>
        <p>
          Before production launch, Hyperboards must confirm the responsible legal entity, privacy
          contact, service providers, retention periods, applicable legal bases and governing
          jurisdictions. Until those details are approved, this page should not be treated as a
          complete statement of legal rights or obligations.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <div class="legal-layout">
        <aside class="legal-index" aria-labelledby="privacy-index-title" data-reveal>
          <h2 id="privacy-index-title">On this page</h2>
          <nav aria-label="Privacy notice sections">
            <a href="#scope">Scope</a>
            <a href="#information">Information submitted</a>
            <a href="#use">Intended use</a>
            <a href="#sharing">Sharing and service providers</a>
            <a href="#retention">Retention and security</a>
            <a href="#rights">Choices and rights</a>
            <a href="#contact">Responsible entity and contact</a>
          </nav>
        </aside>

        <article class="legal-copy" data-reveal>
          <section id="scope">
            <h2>Scope</h2>
            <p>
              This interim notice applies to information submitted through the Hyperboards website,
              including owner, intermediary and investor-relationship inquiries. It does not yet
              describe every practice of the entity that will operate the website.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="information">
            <h2>Information you choose to submit</h2>
            <p>
              An inquiry may include your name, business email, phone number, company, website,
              industry, location, broad EBITDA range and the message you provide. Technical security
              records may also be generated when the form is used.
            </p>
            <div class="note">
              Please do not include customer lists, employee records, account credentials, tax
              records or other highly sensitive documents in an initial inquiry. A website form does
              not itself create a non-disclosure agreement.
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="use">
            <h2>How information is intended to be used</h2>
            <p>Information submitted through the website is expected to be used to:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>review and respond to an introduction;</li>
              <li>consider broad alignment with the published acquisition profile;</li>
              <li>coordinate an appropriate next conversation;</li>
              <li>protect the website, prevent misuse and maintain necessary records; and</li>
              <li>meet legal or regulatory requirements that apply to the responsible entity.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              The final notice will identify the applicable legal bases where required by law.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="sharing">
            <h2>Sharing and service providers</h2>
            <p>
              Inquiry information may need to be handled by the Hyperboards team and limited service
              providers that support hosting, security, form delivery or professional review. The
              final policy must identify the relevant categories, contractual safeguards and any
              cross-border handling after the operating setup is confirmed.
            </p>
            <p>
              Hyperboards should not describe inquiry data as being sold or used for unrelated
              advertising unless the implemented data flow has been reviewed and the final notice
              accurately reflects it.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="retention">
            <h2>Retention and security</h2>
            <p>
              The production service should retain inquiry information only for an approved business,
              legal or security purpose and protect it with controls appropriate to its sensitivity.
              Specific retention periods and deletion practices remain to be confirmed before launch.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="rights">
            <h2>Your choices and legal rights</h2>
            <p>
              Depending on where you live, you may have rights to ask about, access, correct or delete
              personal information, or to object to certain uses. The final notice will explain which
              rights apply, how to exercise them and any appeal or regulator-contact process required
              by the governing jurisdiction.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="contact">
            <h2>Responsible entity and privacy contact</h2>
            <p>
              The legal name and address of the responsible entity, together with a monitored privacy
              email or other contact channel, have not yet been approved for publication. These are
              launch-blocking details and must replace this interim disclosure before the website is
              publicly indexed or used to collect production inquiries.
            </p>
          </section>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    eyebrow="Before you share details"
    title="Start with only the broad facts."
    body="The inquiry page explains what is useful at the introduction stage and what should wait for a protected conversation."
    href="/contact"
    label="Review contact guidance"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    background: var(--color-white);
  }

  .legal-status {
    max-width: 64rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(199, 168, 91, 0.45);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background-color: var(--color-paper);
    background-image: var(--texture-paper);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
  }

  .legal-status h2 {
    max-width: 22ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }

  .legal-status > p:last-child {
    max-width: 53rem;
  }

  .legal-layout {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .legal-index {
    align-self: start;
    padding-top: var(--space-xs);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .legal-index h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .legal-index nav {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  .legal-index a {
    color: var(--color-slate);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    text-decoration-color: transparent;
  }

  .legal-index a:hover {
    color: var(--color-midnight);
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }

  .legal-copy {
    max-width: 49rem;
  }

  .legal-copy section {
    scroll-margin-top: 7rem;
  }

  .legal-copy section + section {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .legal-copy h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }

  .legal-copy li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .legal-copy .note {
    margin-block: var(--space-md);
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .legal-layout {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 0.32fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .legal-index {
      position: sticky;
      top: 7rem;
    }
  }
</style>
